  "summary_md": "Diagnostics & Research names split sharply: cancer-testing companies ride strong volume growth and raised outlooks, while several instrument makers pivot toward AI and robotics themes, often through dilutive financings or reverse mergers. Positive momentum is clearest in **BDSX** and **CSTL**, where accelerating test adoption and upward guidance revisions reflect deepening clinical acceptance, while **XGN** delivered a record quarter in autoimmune diagnostics. At the other extreme, **NOTV** has entered Chapter 11 and faces delisting, and **FCUV** carries a going-concern warning with near-zero revenue, underscoring acute distress. A notable wave of corporate action reshapes the batch: **ELSE** is being acquired at a premium, **SOBR** is executing a reverse merger to become a clean-energy venture, and **VPG** stands out as a profitable beneficiary of the physical AI supercycle, fueled by robotics demand. Across the board, capital raises, listing compliance struggles, and strategic pivots into digital or precision-health themes remain recurring threads.",
  "summary_date": "2026-06-22"
